handoff: Green 3.9 wrote only harness/model-guide/adjudicate.ts. The Red test and the fixtures/review corpus stayed unchanged. The command is `adjudicate.ts queue <set_id> --private <dir> --raw <dir>` and `adjudicate.ts apply <set_id> --private <dir> --judge-a <file> --judge-b <file>`. A missing flag value gives exit 2 and one line `queue: --<flag> needs a value` or `apply: --<flag> needs a value`. The queue writes `<private>/sets/<set_id>/adjudication/queue.json` with exactly set_id and groups. Each group holds id, diff_id, file, window, and items. Each item holds id, line, and the claim text. The queue holds no route name and no verdict. The apply writes verdicts.json and real-defects.json, and it adds a real defect to the key of its diff. The finding ids and the three verdict words match review-score.ts, so the scorer reads the verdicts map of the apply. The apply never marks a plant found. Task 3.10 is [~] for the next Green role. The next role should write harness/model-guide/leak-check.ts and touch no other file.
